# Keeps the build context small and free of local state. The Dockerfile copies an explicit set of files, so anything
# excluded here is simply never sent to the build. This lives at the repository ROOT on purpose: every Docker builder
# honors a root .dockerignore, while a Dockerfile-named one is honored only by BuildKit — so keeping it here means the
# exclusions hold even under the legacy builder. lib/test and lib/scripts are left out on purpose: neither is part of
# the signed release manifest and the runtime never loads either — excluding them also keeps the container's
# self-attest perfectly clean (it reports the signed set with no stray "extra file" to explain). The Dockerfile also
# prunes those two directories after copying lib, as a hard guarantee that does not depend on this file.
.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
src-tauri
lib/test
lib/scripts
.test-data
docs/BACKLOG.md
docs/TEAM-VAULTS-DESIGN.md
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
